@startuml
title Prototype / Clone

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Create new objects by copying a prototype instance.

**Motivation**:
Object creation is expensive or complex; you want to avoid subclasses for configuring instances.

**Applicability**:
Costly or complex initialization; need many similar variants.
Avoids subclassing for diverse configurations.

**Participants**:
Prototype defines clone.
ConcretePrototype implements deep/partial copy.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Fast creation; dynamic configuration; reduce subclass explosion.
Cons: Complex deep-copy semantics; cycles; external resources.

**Implementation Notes**:
Define deep vs. shallow copy semantics explicitly.
Consider copy constructors or serializers for safe cloning.

**Known Uses**:
Java Object#clone() (caveats).
Game engines spawning entities; document editors duplicating elements.

**Related Patterns**:
Factory Method (alternative instantiation), Memento (state capture), Flyweight (shared intrinsic state).

endlegend

interface Prototype {
  +clone() : Prototype
}

class ConcretePrototypeA
class ConcretePrototypeB

Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototypeA
Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototypeB

class Client
Client ..> Prototype : clones
@enduml